Package: piMIMIC
Type: Package
Title: Differential Item Functioning Detection Using MIMIC Models With Product Indicators
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Cesar", "Merino-Soto", email = "sikayax@yahoo.com.ar", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Provides functions to analyze differential item functioning (DIF)
    using the Multiple Indicators Multiple Causes (MIMIC) framework with
    product indicators (PI). The package implements likelihood ratio and
    score tests for global, uniform, and non-uniform DIF detection,
    together with effect size estimation through a fixed-to-zero parameter
    release strategy and R-squared differences. The implementation follows
    the methodology proposed by Kolbe and Jorgensen (see the References
    sections of the documented functions) and utilizes functions from the
    'lavaan' and 'semTools' packages, among others.
